==============================+++++++++++++++++++++++==========================================================

0.0.0.0/0 --> anyone can access from anywhere public access

10.231.156.223  ==> 32 bit IPV4 address with 4 octet means 4 dots here 
4 octets of 8 bits --> 4*8=32 bits
00000000 to 11111111 
255.255.255.255 max and 0.0.0.0 min

2409:4080:e1d:2c4c:94dd:9187:4568:cb28 ==> 8 groups of 16-bit blocks (called hextets, not octets)
8 hextets of 16 bits --> 16*8 =128 bits 


🌐 What is CIDR?
CIDR stands for Classless Inter-Domain Routing.
It's just a short way to write IP ranges.
-> CIDR stands for Classless Inter-Domain Routing.
-> It’s a method for reserving  IP addresses range for a VPC for future allocation to resource for communication between them


CIDR  	      Network Bits  	Host Bits	    Total IPs (2^Host Bits)
/22                 22          10             2^10=>1024  
/23                 23          9              2^9=> 512 
/24	                24         	8	            2^8=> 256
/25	                25	        7          	 2^7=>128
/26	                26        	6	            2^6=>64
/27              	  27	        5	            2^5=>32
/28	                28	        4	            2^4=>16
/30	                30	        2	            2^2=>4

Example1 :- 10.111.11.128/26
-IPv4 contains 32 bit address so from 26 are network bits and remaining are host bits 

calculation :- 2 ^ 32- IP range ==> 2 ^ 32-26 ==> 64 range of IPs
10.111.11.128/26  ==> 128 to 191 
Breakdown -->
Network IP	    10.111.11.128
First Host IP	10.111.11.129
Last Host IP	10.111.11.190

Example 2 :-  10.151.20.0/22  //here it will be divided into 4 subnets bcoz each octet is of 8 bits and one 8 bit contains 256 ip addresss thats why it gets divided into subnets
Breakdown of Subnets in 10.151.20.0/22:
Subnet IP Range  Start IP Range  End IP range    Total IPs
10.151.20.0/24	 10.151.20.0	   10.151.20.255 	    256
10.151.21.0/24	 10.151.21.0	   10.151.21.255	    256
10.151.22.0/24	 10.151.22.0	   10.151.22.255	    256
10.151.23.0/24	 10.151.23.0	   10.151.23.255	    256

